{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:24467-1","published":"2026-10-27T13:55:24Z","modified":"2026-11-04T17:23:17.638422890Z","related":["CVE-2026-93599","CVE-2026-93600","CVE-2026-93601","CVE-2026-93602"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-93599","CVE-2026-93600","CVE-2026-93601","CVE-2026-93602"],"summary":"Security update for aws-nitro-enclaves-cli","details":"This update for aws-nitro-enclaves-cli fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-93599: rustls-webpki: panic in `BorrowedCertRevocationList::from_der` via empty `BIT STRING`\n  in `IssuingDistributionPoint` (bsc#1282250).\n- CVE-2026-93600: rustls-webpki: name constraints for URI names were incorrectly accepted (bsc#1282250).\n- CVE-2026-93601: rustls-webpki: name constraints were accepted for certificates asserting a wildcard name\n  (bsc#1282250).\n- CVE-2026-93602: rustls-webpki: CRLs not considered authoritative by Distribution Point due to faulty matching logic\n  (bsc#1282250).\n- GHSA-7gcf-g7xr-8hxj: serde_with: KeyValueMap serialization panics on empty sequence or map entries (bsc#1271853).\n\nChanges for aws-nitro-enclaves-cli:\n\n- Updated to version 1.5.2\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"aws-nitro-enclaves-cli","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server 16.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/aws-nitro-enclaves-cli&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%2016.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.5.2~git0.1c496ed-160000.1.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"aws-nitro-enclaves-binaryblobs-upstream":"1.5.2~git0.1c496ed-160000.1.1","aws-nitro-enclaves-cli":"1.5.2~git0.1c496ed-160000.1.1","system-group-ne":"1.5.2~git0.1c496ed-160000.1.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:24467-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"aws-nitro-enclaves-cli","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server for SAP applications 16.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/aws-nitro-enclaves-cli&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%20for%20SAP%20applications%2016.